      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 0,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "title": "RefMod Stack example",
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "## RefMod Stack → Text Encode → Ref2VA\n\n1. Click **Browse library…** on the RefMod Stack and add a saved RefMod (a character, place, voice…), or make one with **Create…**. RefMods live in `models/refmods`.\n2. The stack plugs into the Prompt Builder's *mods* input, and the builder passes it on through its *mods* output to Text Encode (in a new workflow, **+ RefMods** on the builder wires this up). Open **Edit prompt…** on the Prompt Builder. The stack's labels appear as chips — `<Picture 1>`, `<Video 1>`, `<Audio 1>` — click one to insert it. The stack's *labels* output and Text Encode's *reference_map* show the same map.\n3. Queue. **Fantastic H3 RefMod Text Encode** presents the references to H3's own encoder, so the prompt can name them; its conditioning already carries the references — do not Apply the same bundle again.\n\nWeights: up to 1 is strength; above 1 adds copies (2.7 = two full + one at 0.7). Every copy gets its own label; citing the first is enough.\n\nModels: [Comfy-Org/MiniMax-H3](https://huggingface.co/Comfy-Org/MiniMax-H3) — ref2va diffusion model, the minimax CLIP, the video VAE and the audio VAE. Swap the filenames below for the variants you have."
      ],
      "color": "#432",
      "bgcolor": "#653"
    },
